%PROPERTIES
Unimodular=1
%REFERENCES
I. Gauvin, Reseaux ideaux pairs unimodulaires de rang 88 sur Q(zeta_115), preprint, 15 October 2026 (arXiv identifier pending).
Data, programs and certificates: https://github.com/Katabolanga/rang88-reseaux-ideaux (input data: commit f20d0bd714a94e0dbb2bf562807dbed1a393dd53).
%NOTES
The two generators span a subgroup of the automorphism group, hence the catalogue sections SUBGROUP_ORDER, SUBGROUP_NAME and SUBGROUP_GENERATORS; the full automorphism group is not known.
SUBGROUP_NAME: C115 : C4 = <zeta> : <g2>, zeta of order 115, g2 of order 4 with g2^2 = -1 and g2^-1 zeta g2 = zeta^24 (C4 acts through C2); equivalently C23 x Dic5.
X139 = (P, b), an ideal lattice over L = Q(zeta), zeta = zeta_115 (rank 88): P = (139, zeta^2 + zeta + 77) is a prime ideal
of Z[zeta] of residue degree 2, and b(u, v) = Tr_{L/Q}(alpha u conj(v)), alpha = beta_0/nu totally positive (see the paper, section 6).
Minimum 8 is established by the computer-assisted theorem of the paper, in the execution model of section 5.4 (M1, M2, H1-H3).
The same enumeration program was run on two computers; the attached Python scripts check the exported matrices and generators, not the minimum.
The kissing number 168498000 follows from that minimum-8 theorem and the extremal theta series.
Basis: an LLL-reduced Z-basis of P; X139_construction.gp gives it in the power basis of Z[zeta], together with alpha.
Generators (row convention, g*GRAM*g^T = GRAM): g1 = multiplication by -zeta, of order 230;
g2 = the semilinear map u -> lambda*sigma_24(u), sigma_24(zeta) = zeta^24, lambda a unit of Z[zeta] (in X139_construction.gp);
g2^2 = -1, and g2 o g1 o g2^(-1) = g1^139 as maps (in matrices: g2^(-1)*g1*g2 = g1^139).
<g1, g2> has order 460 = 2^2*5*23: an extension of the Galois stabiliser <sigma_24> (order 2) of the class of P by the cyclic group
<-zeta> (order 230). By the normaliser argument and the exact Galois stabilisers established in sections 2.4 and 6.4 of the paper
(class-group results, not only these matrices), it is the normaliser in Aut(X139) of the group of multiplications by roots of unity.
The full automorphism group has not been determined: |Aut(X139)| >= 460.
A vector of norm 8 (the witness of the paper, transported to this basis), as a row of coordinates in this basis:
NORM8: -36 30 34 -28 -53 9 31 18 25 -8 -32 -4 -3 -9 27 4 -2 39 -8 4 8 23 -6 -34 -6 0 12 -10 4 -11 -6 16 3 12 -8 12 7 14 -8 6 -8 -1 12 -7 7 -7 -10 2 -4 -1 1 0 4 -2 2 -2 8 4 2 -6 -4 -1 6 4 -1 -7 0 0 1 2 0 -3 5 2 -4 -1 1 2 -3 2 0 4 3 -2 3 1 -1 -1
